<title>USA: Conrail claims Norfolk move may break law.</title>
<headline>Conrail claims Norfolk move may break law.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conrail Inc said on Monday that Norfolk Southern Corp's proposals to gain control of Conrail's board appears to be illegal under U.S. transportation laws.</p>
<p>Also, Conrail said Norfolk Southern's proposals to remove Conrail's incumbent directors and to reduce the number of board members are invalid under Pennsylvania law.</p>
<p>Norfolk Southern was not immediately available for comment.  </p>
<p>&quot;We certainly checked out the legality of everything we do, and legally we're on solid ground,&quot; a Norfolk Southern spokesman said.</p>
</text>
